{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Moses said to the children of Israel.</b> To interrupt the subject — the words of Rabbi Yishmael. For until here they were the words of the Omnipresent, and the passage of vows begins with Moses' speech; it was necessary to interrupt first and say that Moses went back and said this passage to Israel. For otherwise, it would be implied that he did not say this one to them, but in the passage of vows He began His words."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:13:13.936216153Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}